ey":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-15T08:04:31-08:00","id":1547759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1546936-what-are-thou-reading?p=1547700#post1547700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading, <i>The Jews of Khazaria</i>; it's a nice little book about a Turk/Mongol peoples became Jewish and founded a little empire. It's like reading an exotic fantasy novel about a place I've never been too before. It's much more D&amp;D material, than WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you've never read it, you may enjoy Michael Chabon's <i>Gentlemen of the Road</i>, an adventure novel about two 10th century Jewish mercenaries (one Ethiopian, the other German) who end up in Khazaria.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-16T15:57:16-08:00","id":1547784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1546936-what-are-thou-reading?p=1547759#post1547759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you've never read it, you may enjoy Michael Chabon's <i>Gentlemen of the Road</i>, an adventure novel about two 10th century Jewish mercenaries (one Ethiopian, the other German) who end up in Khazaria.</div> </div> </div> </div>It looks like most of the historical-material on Khazaria comes from Spain, actually. The more I read the book, the more I realize that, the Mongols were that special; they were a series of nomadic horsemen that were the Bulgars, the Magyars, the Huns, the Cumans and the Scythians. And, from a D&amp;D OA perspective, I can see the Barbarian-class taking up religion and becoming classic AD&amp;D clerics (it's different in Oriental Adventures).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-13T14:49:33-08:00","id":1548484,"title":"","content":"I'm halfway through Ben Sanderson Bands of Mourning of the Mistborn series and I should Check out some of his other series and see if I will enjoy them and I eagerly await for the next book in Sarah Maas Crescent City series and Miles Cameron alternate Bronze Age series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-14T17:43:21-08:00","id":1548504,"title":"","content":"Read about the origins of Dracula; I took notes, before I realized, I was reading about his father and not him. I think his father's story is a good background for a European-vampire. That is, being an illegitimate-son and having to fight for power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-14T18:52:53-08:00","id":1548508,"title":"","content":"That sounds promising Iguazu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-03T18:49:18-07:00","id":1549797,"title":"","content":"I'm reading a book about the Late Bronze Age Collapse; the Bronze Age collapse was when, all of a sudden, cities (in Greece), stopped building tombs and built wall, and cities were burnt down, and never reoccupied and writing seemed to stop. There was a vast trade network and lots of correspondences between the rulers, etc. Also, there's virtually zero archaeological-evidence of anything that happened in the Bible. And in some cases, the evidence contradicts accounts, such as the Canaanites having more control over certain areas than mentioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-03T22:29:23-07:00","id":1549806,"title":"","content":"I'm currently reading The Necromancer's House by Christopher Buehlman and it's certainly different from what I usually read.<br /> <br /> I also finished reading Alita Battle Angel volume 1-3 omibus and Brandon Sanderson Wax and Wayne Mistborn series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-04-2025, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-27T17:29:16-07:00","id":1550416,"title":"","content":"I'm reading,<i> Lost Christianities</i>; it's about all the stuff that, <i>didn't</i> make it into the Bible. It's very interesting and full of heresies like, the Gospel of Peter; Jesus was immortal and couldn't feel pain/die; Jesus had a twin-brother, Thomas; to get into heaven, women must become a man, then they can enter, etc. I can see why immortal-Jesus, who didn't suffer or die for our sins wouldn't make it into canon-text. I also find it funny, that, when confront with scripture that contradicts what's in the Bible, it's declared an obvious forgery. But, considering the Bible was pieced together hundreds of years after the fact, all gospels and books have a chance to make it in there and be just as valid. Egypt, given it's dry-climate, is perfect for preserving texts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edit