be the last in the series but seems like it may be a branching off point for more I'm not interested in. Pretty generic story except for the &quot;smut&quot; as the author labeled it. Not a lot of books about slime monsters, I was hoping it would do something novel. Don't know what to read next but I have a big enough list to choose from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T00:52:10-07:00","id":1550429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1546936-what-are-thou-reading?p=1550421#post1550421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently I'm reading some <i>Legend of the Five Rings</i> books I didn't had read yet, for a game I'll run in its 4th edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got Oriental Adventures 3e that's based of of Legend of the Five-Rights; I like the new races, much, better production and graphics, but, the old AD&amp;D Original version of Oriental Adventures, is better written and easier to understand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T10:38:45-07:00","id":1550453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1546936-what-are-thou-reading?p=1550429#post1550429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've got Oriental Adventures 3e that's based of of Legend of the Five-Rights; I like the new races, much, better production and graphics, but, the old AD&amp;D Original version of Oriental Adventures, is better written and easier to understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>3rd ed Oriental Adventures was the result of a partnership between AEG and WotC that, imho, didn't served well neither.<br /> <br /> Only some specific parts of it are based on L5R, by the way, and it doesn't include most of the new races. L5R is heavily geared towards humans, focusing on the distinction between the clans.<br /> <br /> But that's all L5R 2nd Ed anyway. I'm reading 4th ed, which was the final and best version of their proprietary Roll and Keep system under AEG. I'm also interested in the new 5th Ed by FFG, but due to circumstances the game I'll run will be 4th ed.<br /> <br /> I strongly recommend L5R as a read, at least the Core Book. It isn't just an amazing setting (although one with problems, as it is a terrible case of orientalism), it's also a very interesting system to contrast with the Storyteller System, specially pertaining to social mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T14:33:51-07:00","id":1550464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1546936-what-are-thou-reading?p=1550453#post1550453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3rd ed Oriental Adventures was the result of a partnership between AEG and WotC that, imho, didn't served well neither.<br /> <br /> Only some specific parts of it are based on L5R, by the way, and it doesn't include most of the new races. L5R is heavily geared towards humans, focusing on the distinction between the clans.<br /> <br /> But that's all L5R 2nd Ed anyway. I'm reading 4th ed, which was the final and best version of their proprietary Roll and Keep system under AEG. I'm also interested in the new 5th Ed by FFG, but due to circumstances the game I'll run will be 4th ed.<br /> <br /> I strongly recommend L5R as a read, at least the Core Book. It isn't just an amazing setting (although one with problems, as it is a terrible case of orientalism), it's also a very interesting system to contrast with the Storyteller System, specially pertaining to social mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooo, I forgot about the clans! That's the best part of 3e OA; AD&amp;D's OA was always geared towards humans and that spices it up, a bit. Also, D&amp;D's OA, has a terrible case of Orientalism; they've literally lumped Japan in with China's customs and beliefs; but they got one thing right; all you do is eat rice!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-29T04:18:50-07:00","id":1550477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1546936-what-are-thou-reading?p=1550424#post1550424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is it? I don't normally read fanfic but for horror stuff I make exceptions.<br /> <br /> I just finished up Black Melt: Mother Fountain, which I thought would be the last in the series but seems like it may be a branching off point for more I'm not interested in. Pretty generic story except for the &quot;smut&quot; as the author labeled it. Not a lot of books about slime monsters, I was hoping it would do something novel. Don't know what to read next but I have a big enough list to choose from.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bizarre trainwreck of a fic called &quot;Resident Evil: Behind The Mask&quot;, posted to Archive Of Our Own by a guy with the username MordredOfBritannia. It's 50 chapters long and it's a doozy. A trainwreck but an entertaining trainwreck that takes me back to the good old days of Fanfiction.net and all that jazz.<br /> <br /> Be forewarned, it contains a LOT of violence, gore, harsh language, conspiracy theories, and some chapters contain nudity and sexual content as well. It's very much R-rated, so reader discretion is advised.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 04-29-2025, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-30T23:15:21-07:00","id":1550534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1546936-what-are-thou-reading?p=1550477#post1550477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a bizarre trainwreck of a fic called &quot;Resident Evil: Behind The Mask&quot;, posted to Archive Of Our Own by a guy with the username MordredOfBritannia. It's 50 chapters long and it's a doozy. A trainwreck but an entertaining trainwreck that takes me back to the good old days of Fanfiction.net and all that jazz.<br /> <br /> Be forewarned, it contains a LOT of violence, gore, harsh language, conspiracy theories, and some chapters contain nudity and sexual content as well. It's very much R-rated, so reader discretion is advised.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the response! It looks right up my alley. And it's finished! Which seems a rarity in longer series. I'm a big horror lit reader so all those tags are just flames to my moth.<br /> <br /> It's even crossed over with Cardcaptor, a series I tried to get into decades ago but seemed too saccharine. Sounds like a good one!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T15:08:04-07:00","id":1550610,"title":"","content":"I finished reading Brad Thor The Apostle thriller book and now back to some Historical Fiction by Simon Scarrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-05T17:34:48-07:00","id":1551486,"title":"","content":"I'm currently reading The Icarus Job by the always good Timothy Zahn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T12:06:38-07:00","id":1552161,"title":"","content":"Reading: <i>Life and Labor in the Old South</i>; it's about, you guessed it, the South from early-colonial times to the 1800's, thus far. It's has great material if you want to run a game based in the Old South from descriptions of the weather, roads, houses, slaves and the economic-impacts etc. I'm reading it at college libraries and also online:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://archive.org/details/in.ernet.dli.2015.229114/page/n179/mode/2up\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://archive.org/services/img/in.ernet.dli.2015.229114\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://archive.org/details/in.ernet.dli.2015.229114/page/n179/mode/2up\" target=\"_blank\"> Life And Labor In The Old South : Ulrich Bonnell Phillips : Free Download, Borrow, and Streaming : Internet Archive </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://archive.org/details/in.ernet.dli.2015.229114/page/n179/mode/2up\" target=\"_blank\"> https://archive.org/details/in.ernet.dli.2015.229114/page/n179/mode/2up </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Book Source: Digital Library of India Item 2015.229114dc.contributor.author: Ulrich Bonnell Phillipsdc.date.accessioned: 2015-07-10T15:52:54Zdc.date.available:... </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T17:15:42-07:00","id":1552176,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing it's about the Old South of the US, but is it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T18:05:39-07:00","id":1552180,"title":"","content":"I'm reading Conn Iggudun Genghis Khan series right now. This writer is quite excellent for the historical fiction genre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-13T10:05:52-07:00","id":1552333,"title":"","content":"<i>Life and Labor of the Old South </i>has a very good description of the peoples of New Orleans; thanks to Ann Rice, New Orleans is now a vampire-haven as much as Bram Stroker made Transylvania a haven for vampires. I'm thinking of designing a city based off of New Orleans. I'm working on a map based off of South Carolina; I'm designing, &quot;Charelston&quot;, but, I've never looked at a map of Charleston; I'm just designing the city with the space it occupied, with the sprites I have and the capacity of the program. And it's not for a Requiem-game; it's the start of a Foresaken-game. <br /> <br /> And, the author of the book, has to compare paying alimony, to slavery; online, it's a pain in the rear to flip the pages back and see when it was written, but I'm guessing near the 1950's.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1546936-what-are-thou-reading?p=1552176#post1552176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing it's about the Old South of the US, but is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes,; it's about the Antebellum-South, thus far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-21T16:56:17-07:00","id":1552568,"title":"","content":"And the book was first written in 1928, then published again, by his wife 1959.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T12:14:15-07:00","id":1553111,"title":"","content":"I finished reading The End and The Death by Dan Abbent from the Siege of Terra storyline from Warhammer 40 K and I found it engaging as he did a good job considering how many characters are involved. But he focused on the main characters primarily and only brought in the supporting and minor characters when needed or made sense.<br /> <br /> For example it made perfect sense that Ahriman of the Thousand Sons would be there to try to get as much historical and occult lore that he could get his hands on as he is a scholar first and solider second like his legion and doesn't really trust Horus being any better inclined to the sons of Magnus then the Imperium was.<br /> <br /> It good moments of writing like this that gives me hope that writing isn't a fading artform.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T17:54:20-07:00","id":1553121,"title":"","content":"Oh, writing definitely isn't a fading artform. Quite the opposite, more people are engaging with it than ever. The types and medias aren't always traditional, but there's still more writers than ever to be found and start new careers. Even with more and more digital books every year, the market for paper books is slowly increasing again, and new talent show up in places like Reddit and TikTok all the time with short stories (and not so short ones).<br /> <br /> There are lots of things I'm worrying about nowadays, even some related to the new generations, but writing going out of favor really isn't one of those.<br /> <br /> Well, personally I'm right now starting Geist 2nd Ed. Mummy took me quite some time to understand to my heart's content.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-16T08:30:35-07:00","id":1553217,"title":"","content":"Just finished a book about the ancient Maya; it was written by an anthropologists, not a Mayan-historian. so, it's more technical and more detailed with lots of science to back up the facts; for instance, the Mayan didn't starve when their civilization-collapsed; oxygen-isotopes on skeletons confirmed they were as well fed as those in the past. <br /> <br /> What gets me the most, that applies a lot to CoD, is their ritual blood-letting. Doesn't that scream vampire? But, what if, there were no vamps there during that time? I mean, what if, vamps were strictly Old World, and their blood letting so for something different? Someone like a Blood-bather? <br /> <br /> Sorry Shadows of Mexico, but, the old-Mexico may not have been as Foresaken/Requiem paradise as depicted in the book. Vampires would have a real hard time getting to the Americas*. Even Gangrel would have difficulties even with Earth-Meld, unless they crossed the Bering land-bridge (which would make them old, really old). Or, to avoid the Sun, one walked, under water. The People, not so much. They could have gotten by boat, or, really did cross the Land-bridge. <br /> <br /> And while reading the book, I couldn't help but think they'll be America's future (USA). A collapsed civilization with ruins everywhere, with people living in isolated tribes. I mean, we're using the resources of the entire planet to support our lifestyle; this can't go on forever. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Or perhaps, they had a real hard time leaving the Americas for Eurasia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-23T13:23:00-07:00","id":1553404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1546936-what-are-thou-reading?p=1553217#post1553217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What gets me the most, that applies a lot to CoD, is their ritual blood-letting. Doesn't that scream vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> Mayan ritual bloodletting actually bled less than medical bloodletting and then burn it, and medical bloodletting was an extremely common practice everywhere until the very end of the 19th century, despite little evidence of effectiveness, so I'd say bloodletting says more about the presence of vampires in other places (including Europe, but it was common in every inhabited continent) than among the Mayans, unless it's a magic ritual made either by or against vampires.<br /> <br /> And remember that Requiem's vampires aren't descended from a single original vampire. Vampires from America (continent) and Europe may have appeared independently, and probably did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-30T04:09:26-07:00","id":1553552,"title":"","content":"Going back to my old stomping grounds on Fanfiction Dot Net and I fucking love it. Really takes me back.<br /> <br /> Currently reading an old Bleach fanfic called &quot;Rukia's Curiosity&quot; that I remember reading way back in 2009.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-04T20:07:42-07:00","id":1553632,"title":"","content":"I'm readying myself to look for a good translation of <i>Journey to the West</i>. I've read plenty of summaries on it, but never the full text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-05T11:39:00-07:00","id":1553644,"title":"","content":"I'm reading Marked For Death The Lost Mark by Matt Forbeck. As a side note I was friends with him on Facebook and he was nice to me and gave me advice on writing short stories, even though I'm not on Facebook, Snapchat, Twitter or Instagram at all. It was a good experience for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-17T22:10:29-07:00","id":1553891,"title":"","content":"I'm just starting to read Framed by John Grisham and Jim McCloskey that covers true stories of wrongful convictions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-18T04:31:24-07:00","id":1553896,"title":"","content":"I've just finished Hamattan Season by Tochi Onyebuchi. It's sort-of a fantasy-noir-mystery but the most interesting element was its setting of colonial West Africa (under French occupation at the time). I think this one was really a case of &quot;lesser than the sum of its parts&quot;. I've liked pretty much all about it, the characters, the setting, the story... but oh man, the pacing of the plot. To describe the plot as moving at breakneck speed is an understatement. There's even a moment in the middle where the protagonist thinks about how he can't believe that this all started with a dead girl. Looking back on it, I really did feel like the protagonist couldn't walk five meters without him rushing headlong into another plot-point. <br /> <br /> But I'm really excited to dig into Hemlock &amp; Silver by T. Kingfisher. I heard good things about the writer but for some reason I've never picked up one of their books before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-21T08:32:50-07:00","id":1553954,"title":"","content":"Russia: Under the Old Regime by Richard Pipes; its interesting and readable. I have to go to a college library to read it; the city ones don't have anything about Russia other than modern-stuff. Its like I'm going back to a time and world that is completely different than most histories, which are European.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-23T04:31:24-07:00","id":1553973,"title":"","content":"I've started re-reading The Long Walk. I read it years ago and absolutely loved it, so I thought I'd revisit it before I see the movie (which I'm pretty excited to see).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-01T16:33:24-07:00","id":1554089,"title":"","content":"I decided to pick H.P. Lovecraft's Necronomicon and see how generations of horror writers were inspired to pick up the pen so to speak. It's also interesting to see a glimpse of the attitudes of the writers back in the day and seeing how much society has changed and not changed in some aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-01T19:36:24-07:00","id":1554096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1546936-what-are-thou-reading?p=1554089#post1554089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I decided to pick H.P. Lovecraft's Necronomicon</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no such book.<br /> <br /> Lovecraft never wrote an actual version of the book, it only exists as references within his stories.<br /> <br /> You can find books entitled <i>Necronomicon</i>, but they're far later works. While they're homages to Lovecraft, they have nothing to do with the authors of Lovecraft's time. The earliest of those books are from the 50's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-02T11:07:02-07:00","id":1554105,"title":"","content":"While true Monteparnas, this is the first time I read anything from H.P. Lovecraft and his fellow writers like Arthur Manchen, Lafcadio Hearn or Robert W. Chambers and it makes for interesting reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-02T16:53:31-07:00","id":1554111,"title":"","content":"I'd like to know which <i>Necronomicon</i> you're reading.<br /> <br /> But Lovecraft does make for a good reading. I'm particularly fond of <i>At The Mountains of Madness</i>, but he has a lot of other wonderful works. You only have to be wary of his many problematic stances, as they're all over the place in his works. <i>The Call of Cthulhu</i> isn't a classic for nothing and is a short read, a must read, but it's also especially riddled with racism to the point that I know Lovecraft fans that couldn't finish reading it due to sheer disgust.<br /> <br /> On the bright side of things, Lovecraft was part of a literary movement that prized the free sharing of ideas, and never claimed ownership of anything he created. In a sense he was one of the earliest adopters of the concept of Creative Commons. So you can enjoy his creations in all kinds of flavors and variations in works that date back to the time of the originals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-02T17:43:25-07:00","id":1554112,"title":"","content":"It's from Arcturus Publishing and it's from this year Monteparnas.<br /> <br /> To your point on the racial overtones, I wish people would grow a thicker skin and stop judging older societies and there works of art through presentism.<br /> <br /> A writer that was born in 1890 A D is going to have views that were common at the time and be seen as shocking by later generations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 10-02-2025, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-03T11:00:24-07:00","id":1554123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1546936-what-are-thou-reading?p=1554112#post1554112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's from Arcturus Publishing and it's from this year Monteparnas.<br /> <br /> To your point on the racial overtones, I wish people would grow a thicker skin and stop judging older societies and there works of art through presentism.<br /> <br /> A writer that was born in 1890 A D is going to have views that were common at the time and be seen as shocking by later generations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahn... no.<br /> <br /> First, depending on the situation it's perfectly acceptable to say a work didn't age well. <i>Presentism</i>, while a thing, is more often than not an excuse to not discuss an actual problem. If a work is racist, what's the problem in pointing out that it is racist? And if someone can't stand it, why should this person be judged for &quot;not having a thicker skin&quot;? Reading isn't an obligation.<br /> <br /> But in this case it's worse. Lovecraft was <u><b>not</b></u> a common member of his society. He was seen as a hateful bigot with no tolerance for diversity <u><b>by his peers</b></u>. He was pretty vocal about his prejudices and extremely critical of how NYC in his time was permissive of things he deemed complete degeneracy, like mixed race people living in the open as human beings.<br /> <br /> We're literally talking about a man the Ku Klux Klan publicly deemed an extremist in the 20's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-04T15:42:15-07:00","id":1554146,"title":"","content":"Even the KKK didn't want him? That's an incredible achievement to obtain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-04T15:45:21-07:00","id":1554147,"title":"","content":"On a good note, I finished reading The book from H.P. Lovecraft and his fellow writers and moved to Jade War by Fonda Lee volume 2 and find it as good as the first one though I have to refresh myself from the first novel to remember the main characters and what the storyline had left off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T12:16:12-07:00","id":1554164,"title":"","content":"Read Edgar Allen Poe's <i>Gold Bug</i>; OK, so, did Poe want to impress his readers with his decoding and ciphering? When he dug that hole, looking for, &quot;Treasure&quot;, I thought he was going to throw the narrator in it and bury him alive. No, it's about Capt. Kidd and about how pirates buried the diggers too, to keep a secret, but I already knew that. Say, question, when did watches become a thing? They mentioned they found watches, in 1843, so that means they had to be around since pirate-times? Or was that just a familiar allusion for the time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T04:49:48-07:00","id":1554414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1546936-what-are-thou-reading?p=1554164#post1554164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">did Poe want to impress his readers with his decoding and ciphering?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, yes, that was precisely that, and they knew. He specifically wrote The Gold-Bug after publishing a work on secret codes and the public's response showing there was a big interest on the topic.<br /> <br /> Notice also that cryptography was little known and seen as almost magical at the time. We have a lot more familiarity with it today, but his public was really impressed even by the simplest ciphers. Just to be clear, this is not a &quot;past&quot; thing, this is specifically a &quot;19th century&quot; thing, as the use and understanding of ciphers waxed and waned through history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1546936-what-are-thou-reading?p=1554164#post1554164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but I already knew that.</div> </div> </div> </div>For whatever it's worth, The Gold-Bug is among the <i>precursors</i> of the detective story. On top of the cipher thing, a lot of <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/SeinfeldIsUnfunny\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Seinfeld&quot; Is Unfunny - TV Tropes</a> applies.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1546936-what-are-thou-reading?p=1554164#post1554164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">when did watches become a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200bEarly 16th century, becoming popular mid 17th, which is around the same time the Golden Age of Piracy began.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T11:44:29-07:00","id":1554484,"title":"","content":"If anyone is interested in the development of watches, I highly recommend Dava Sobel's book <b>Longitude</b>, about the quest to develop proper maritime chronometers. (Being able to accurately know the time of both your current location and that of the port you left from is necessary for determining longitude, and the older pendulum or water powered clocks don't work properly on ships. The Portuguese, Spanish, French, and English governments were offering massive amounts of money to anyone who could solve the problem as far back as the 1500s.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T22:44:14-07:00","id":1554508,"title":"","content":"I finished reading Ahriman Undying from John French which has everyone's favorite Thousand Sons mystic trying once again to undo his mistakes of saving his fellow &quot;brothers&quot; from a ritual that he cast long ago to save them from uncontrollable mutations and making things usually worse.<br /> <br /> You want him to have a redemption arc, but then you remember all the horrible things he has done to learn the knowledge he needs to fix his mistakes.<br /> <br /> This is why I like Ahriman and the Thousand Sons legion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T19:19:55-07:00","id":1554629,"title":"","content":"I read the first few pages at a local-library; I like older-books because, sometimes, I can find them online. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://ia801404.us.archive.org/27/items/in.ernet.dli.2015.110576/2015.110576.The-Russian-Empire-1801-1917.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-im