e":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-06T18:21:14-08:00","id":1555192,"title":"","content":"<b>Titan Shrinking</b> by James Dixon, looking at the history of the WWE (nee WWF) in 1992, including the various steroid trials and multiple sexual abuse scandals. (Honestly, I think the only thing that kept Vince McMahon out of prison at this time was the sheer incompetence of the Department of Justice and various state agencies.) Dixon has previously done a trilogy about the years 1995 to 1997 (Sinking, Shattered, and Screwed, respectively), and this is the first part of a new trilogy about the years leading up to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-06T18:26:45-08:00","id":1555193,"title":"","content":"That I can believe about the early steroid case in 1992 about Vincent MacMahon of how they underestimated the resources that WWF had at its disposal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T20:52:23-08:00","id":1555388,"title":"","content":"Lies Weeping, by Glen Cook. I was a little worried when it was announced. The Black Company series are flat out my favorite books but their story basically ended with Soldiers Live back in 2000. It's so good, though, I'm really enjoying it. It's doing a great job at illuminating a lot of the backstory of the series and drawing out new plot threads for the present and future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-04T21:23:54-08:00","id":1556163,"title":"","content":"An Eye For An Eye by Jeffrey Archer from his William Warrick series and how vengeance is a fool's errand with the main villain Miles Faulkner after getting released from jail is already plotting his war against the Warrick family and even his lawyer Booth Watson who is hardly Mr. Ethical is tired of it and wants his client to move on as they're not getting any younger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-07T11:03:04-08:00","id":1557367,"title":"","content":"I just finished reading The Fallen Stars by Imani Erriu and while I normally don't go out of my way to read romantic fantasy as I prefer Mystery/Suspense, Thrillers, Historical Fiction and Urban Fantasy myself. I will find some of authors of the genre do attract my interest by plot description and if I find the first couple of chapters hold my interest.<br /> <br /> This is one case that it did as it had gods, magic, suspense and likeable flawed characters. I'm not going to ruin the plot but I think people should check out Imani Erriu work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-11T18:59:05-08:00","id":1558250,"title":"","content":"<i>Iraq: Power &amp; Society:</i> it's a book about the modern-history of Iraq; years ago, I created a little vampire-society, in North-Africa / Middle-East based off of Talonsoft's Western Front graphics, that took place the 1940's (but, with Night-Edge Vampires instead of V:tM). The a few years after that, I read Salman Rashide's Satanic-Verses, and with WoD: Book of Spirits and reading Ann Rice's works, that REALLY got me thinking. Reading that book ('bout Iraq), now I am thinking of a 1950's WoD-game, but with a vampire, as queen of the region (probably not Iraq, but, similar); she is queen and recognized by the British-government: so we have an actual vampire, as head of a mortal-state. And yes, being in a very religious-region, there's gonna be problems. I am thinking of all sorts of NPCs to add to the mix from wealthy land-owners, to tribesmen etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-12T16:24:48-08:00","id":1558266,"title":"","content":"The Jade Legacy by Fonda Lee which takes place in a alternate world with advanced technology and mystic martial arts via Jade Stones where only a handful of people can safely use them and how it can be a cause of much strain as the various jade using clans on the island nation of Kenko (I know I misspelled it) are the ruling factions and control almost everything and in many ways act part corporation and part organized crime outfit and when they fight over turf and honor. It's the regular people who will suffer and in the 3rd and final book many people in the nation and in the world have had enough of these groups. It makes for good reading about the nature of power and what it will show about a person's true nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thra